WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.529
When the 2018 iPad Pro was released, the most
disappointing thing about it was the software.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:11.480
But today, Apple has announced iPadOS, a new
operating system that allows iPads to be more

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.480
like computers.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.720
It’s coming this September, and it supports
every iPad since the iPad Air 2.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.720
Let’s get right into the changes.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.110
First of all, there’s a new home screen
that holds 6 columns of apps instead of 5

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:26.650
currenty on iOS 12, and they can all slide
over to the side to make room for the new

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.860
Today View with customizable widgets, all
on one page.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.359
iOS 13’s new Dark Mode is also coming to
iPadOS.

00:00:34.359 --> 00:00:37.710
It turns on easily from the control center
and it works systemwide.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:43.069
Apple’s also making it super easy for third-party
apps to support it with their new SwitchUI

00:00:43.069 --> 00:00:44.069
framework.

00:00:44.069 --> 00:00:49.909
Face ID on the iPad Pro will unlock up to
30% faster, and apps will be smaller in size

00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:53.670
so they’ll download faster and launch up
to 2x faster than before.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:59.459
The Photos app gets a new Photos tab, which
organizes your photos in new day, month and

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:00.499
year views.

00:01:00.499 --> 00:01:05.229
We also finally have some awesome photo editing
tools, allowing you to adjust things like

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:08.979
brightness, contrast, saturation, and white
balance.

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:14.140
You get those same tools for video editing
as well, alongside auto enhance, crop and

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.140
rotate.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.149
Yes, you can finally rotate videos.

00:01:17.149 --> 00:01:23.020
With iPadOS, Safari automatically chooses
the desktop version of websites and it automatically

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.439
optimizes it for touch.

00:01:24.439 --> 00:01:29.549
There’s also a brand new download manager
that saves downloads right into the new Downloads

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:34.320
Folder within the Files app, making it much
more like an actual computer.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:38.500
And speaking of the Files app, it’s now
actually decent and more computer-like than

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:44.390
ever before by FINALLY allowing you to connect
an external hard drive, SD Card or USB flash

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.299
drive and transfer files.

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:51.399
The biggest deal is the new On My iPad location
which allows you to create folders and transfer

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:56.390
files directly to those folders without having
to first import them to camera roll or put

00:01:56.390 --> 00:02:00.470
them on the iCloud drive, so it’s basically
like a MacOS file manager.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.409
You can even zip and unzip files and folders.

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:08.410
Another big step up is that you can now connect
a digital camera and import files directly

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:12.980
into apps like Lightroom, without having to
copy them to camera roll first like we had

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:13.980
to before.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:18.470
For cloud storage, you can now share files
and entire folders with other people, and

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:23.440
we even get support for Shared servers, so
if you have a cloud-accessible NAS, you can

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.580
access those files on your iPad.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:29.800
And finally, there’s a new column view that
makes it easy to navigate through folders,

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:35.860
and a preview pane that gives you detailed
metadata with quick actions like markup, rotate

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:37.510
and create PDF.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.030
Apple has also taken the iPad a step further
by adding the same keyboard shortcuts we get

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:48.070
on MacOS, right onto the iPad using the smart
keyboard or any compatible Bluetooth keyboard.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:52.840
You can now also download custom fonts right
from the app store and manage them on the

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:53.840
iPad.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.150
The most annoying thing to do while browsing
the web is creating new accounts and passwords,

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:03.690
well now Apple is adding a new Sign in with
Apple feature that automatically and instantly

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:10.200
creates accounts using your existing Apple
ID with a simple Face ID or Touch ID confirmation.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.310
And there’s even an option to create a unique
fake email address that forwards to your real

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.050
email, so it adds tons security as well.

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:22.490
The iPad can also be used to encrypt your
HomeKit Security video cameras footage so

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:25.940
you know that no one else is able to hack
in and view your cameras feed

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:30.910
Apple has also completely redesigned the text
editing, with brand new gestures that are

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:33.230
so much easier to understand and use.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:38.090
To move the cursor while, editing, just touch
and drag it to your desired location.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:41.740
To select a block of text, just drag your
finger over it.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:44.720
You can also select text using multiple taps.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.600
Two taps for a word.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:50.020
Three for a sentence, and four taps for an
entire paragraph.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:55.320
Once selected, pinch with three fingers to
copy, then spread with three fingers to paste.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:04:00.030
And there’s no more need to shake your iPad
to undo, now simply swipe with three fingers

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.030
instead.

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:05.860
Apple has also added no on-screen keyboard
features, like the new Quickpath, or swipe,

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:10.740
keyboard, and the ability to pink and shrink
the keyboard to detach it and move it wherever

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.580
you want for one-handed typing.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:17.070
Now onto multitasking, Apple has added some
additional options to easily switch between

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.680
the app that’s open in slide over mode.

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:23.750
Simply swipe up on the bar on the bottom of
the app and every previous app you’ve had

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:25.040
open pops up.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.680
You can even slide along the bar to swipe
between slide over apps, just like you can

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:31.800
do on the home bar for full-screen apps.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:36.030
Another huge update that makes the iPad more
like a Mac is the ability to open multiple

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:42.660
windows of the same app, so that means two
Notes apps, two mail apps, or even two third-party

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.540
apps like Microsoft word, side by side.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:50.120
This also means that you can have multiple
split-screen spaces open with multiple instances

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.910
of the same apps running at the same time.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:56.930
And to view those spaces, just tap on an app
on the dock and it’ll show you all of the

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.530
spaces that include that app.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:02.850
Apple has also made it easier to work with
the Apple Pencil, with a new easy way to markup

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.330
a photo or page.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.770
Just drag your apple pencil from the corner
of the screen to mark up.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:13.490
And there’s also an awesome new Full Page
option which actually includes the whole full-length

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:17.820
page you’re viewing, not just the section
that was visible when you started the markup.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.880
Within markup, there’s a new pencil tool
pallete with updated icons.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.860
You can easily shrink or drag and move the
palette anywhere you’d like so it doesn’t

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:26.860
get in your way.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:29.700
Now here’s an outstanding new feature called
sidecar.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:34.560
You can now use your iPad as a second Mac
display, allowing you to view an app on the

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.730
iPad while working on your Mac, or exactly
the opposite.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:44.389
You can actually use your iPad to draw, design,
edit or create content using Full desktop

00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:47.310
Mac apps while viewing the finished result
on your Mac.

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.770
And it even works wirelessly.

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:53.830
Alongside all of those awesome changes to
the iPad, Apple has a massive list of changes

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:58.060
that are coming with iPadOS, and I’ll share
that link in the video description below.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:00.060
But here are some of the coolest changes.

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:04.700
The iPad now supports the PS4 and Xbox One
S gaming controller.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:08.520
The 2018 iPad Pro now supports Dolby Atmos
playback.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:14.110
You can now select WiFi networks and Bluetooth
accessories straight from the control center.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.220
You can now add attachments to events in Calendar.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:20.400
Maps is completely redesigned to include more
detail.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.480
Siri has a brand new voice.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.960
You can now control your entire iPad using
a new voice control feature.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.310
And there’s just so much more than that,
so if this video helped you out, make sure

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:32.020
to tap like and click that button above to
subscribe.

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:40.320
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video!

